// TEST: Tuple Equality Width Mismatch (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3001
// ERROR-CONTAINS: (Int64, Int64, Int64)
// ============================================================================
// Comparing tuples of different WIDTHS is a type mismatch, refused in the
// front end. C++ has no `operator==` across widths at all, so without this the
// program type-checked clean and died in g++ as a page of <tuple> template
// instantiation errors naming a header the user never wrote -- and on the
// interpreter lane it died later still, at run time.
//
// BL3001 rather than a new code because that is what it is: the width of a
// tuple-typed name is STATIC (Design C, `004`), so two widths are two types.
// ============================================================================
let r = (2, 3) == (2, 3, 4)
// EXPECT: typecheck failure -- a 2-tuple and a 3-tuple are different types
